<title>FRANCE: Bouygues in Internet deal with AOL.</title>
<headline>Bouygues in Internet deal with AOL.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bouygues Telecom, a unit of Bouygues, said it had signed a deal with Internet service provider AOL to give its mobile telephone users access to AOL and the Internet.</p>
<p>It said that the alliance aimed at offering all kinds of multimedia products by linking the mobile telecommunications technology with online services.</p>
<p>AOL is a joint venture between America Online and Mannesmann. Bouygues Telecom is operating France's third mobile telephone network using the DCS 1,800 standard.</p>
</text>
